.env
.env.*
!.env.example
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Service account keys must never be committed, under any name.
#
# The narrow patterns below were not enough once: "trading.json" was listed
# while the real file was called "trading-journal.json", which sat untracked
# and one `git add -A` away from being published. A service account is a
# full-access credential — there is no undoing that. So the rules are broad
# now, and the project's own files are allowlisted back in by name.
*serviceAccount*.json
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
trading.json
trading-journal.json
*credentials*.json
*-key.json
*.pem
